<title>RUSSIA: RUSSIA'S GROSS GRAIN CROP 28.6 MLN T AT AUG 11.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA'S GROSS GRAIN CROP 28.6 MLN T AT AUG 11.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's grain harvest totalled 28.6 million tonnes bunker weight as of August 11, a drop of around four percent on year-ago levels, official figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The State Statistics Committee released the following data on the progress of the harvest:</p>
<p>	 PROGRESS IN RUSSIAN GRAIN HARVEST AS OF AUG 11</p>
<p>		    (Grains, not including maize)</p>
<p>					    1997     1996     1995</p>
<p>Threshed (million tonnes,</p>
<p>	     bunker weight)	   28.6     29.8     32.2</p>
<p>  Cut (million hectares)		  14.9     18.7     23.6</p>
<p>  Cut (as pct of sown area)	 31.2     38.8     47.9</p>
<p>  Threshed (million hectares)	   13.0     17.1     22.2</p>
<p>  Threshed (as pct of sown area)  27.2     35.5     45.1</p>
<p>  Threshed (as pct of cut area)   87.1     91.4     94.2</p>
<p>  Yields per hectare (tonnes)     2.21     1.74     1.45</p>
<p>It said around 80 percent of grain crops in the Northern Caucasus, which accounts for up to 40 percent of Russia's free-market grain supplies at the end of the harvest, had been cut.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
